"""Authoring guidance for protocol 2.0 (blind no-ref); 1.0 specs keep their historical rendering."""

STYLE_VERSION = "benchmark-concise-3-blind-1"
HISTORICAL_STYLE_VERSION = "benchmark-concise-2-direct-add-1"

INSTRUCTION_STYLE = """BENCHMARK-CONCISE-3 AUTHORING:
Write ONE imperative sentence: action + minimal unambiguous target + required result. Use protocol templates: Add <item> <relation> <anchor>; Replace <target> with <replacement>; Remove <target>; Change the <property> of <target> to <value>; Tint <target> <color>; Make <target> <opacity>.
REFERENCE: Produce ONE compact noun phrase, not a noun followed by a second description. Start with the actual object/part noun. If unique, STOP. Otherwise choose the shortest VERIFIED modifier that excludes the closest similar instance: an adjective, possessive, ordinal in a visible group, or short prepositional phrase. Prefer "the middle cup", "the leftmost window", "the right man's shirt", "the hand holding the swab" when these are sufficient and true. Do not routinely combine host + appearance + position. Do not append ", which is ...", ", located ...", "the one ...", parentheses, or an exclusion list. An essential landmark belongs inside the noun phrase: "the petal immediately above the lowest leaf". Keep a second modifier ONLY when the first still matches a rival. Never shorten a part to its whole host, guess an ordinal, or omit a necessary counting group/direction. Typical simple references need only 3-8 English words; this is guidance, not a limit.
EDIT: State only requested result-defining details. Add needs item/count and a direct relation; site is EMPTY unless a particular host part is necessary. Reference locators identify the host; site locates the addition. Do not repeat either. Replace uses ONE complete new-object noun phrase including its changed physical form: "a square four-hole button", not "a button with a square button design featuring four holes". Attribute names the property and value without restating the current appearance. Remove names the deletion extent without inpainting instructions.
PUBLIC VS INTERNAL: Put rival comparisons, fallback reasons and form-change evidence in their internal fields, never in the instruction or keep/qualifier. All requested result details must remain in the public result phrase. Keep/qualifier defaults to empty; generic preservation of shape, texture, lighting and other details is already implicit. Only retain a short scope-critical preservation clause if omitting it would change the requested result. Exact inscription text remains literal data.
FINAL SILENT CHECK: Read the whole rendered sentence and remove every word/phrase that neither distinguishes the target nor defines the requested result. Fold necessary location into the noun phrase instead of adding a clause. Recheck against the nearest rival in the unmarked scene. Aim for Ref <=26 English words and No-ref <=16, without padding to those budgets. Never truncate, delete essential scope/placement/counts/text, or reject merely for length. No-ref is BLIND: split the sentence into "where" and "what"; the whole "where" (category, part, host, add site, position, ordinal, current appearance) becomes "the selected region" and the source mask is exactly that region (for add: the attachment site); the "what" (action, payload, property and value, relation, result phrase) stays verbatim. This check is inside this one model request, not another call."""


ADD_ANCHOR_POLICY = """ADD ANCHOR PRIORITY (naturalness and precise interaction both matter):
1. First try an ordinary addition DIRECTLY supported by, attached to, contained in, worn on, or printed on the actual selected object/surface. The selected mask should indicate where the addition belongs, not merely an object used to describe distant empty space. Choose the item to suit this host's function, material, scale and visible available space. A cushion on a seat, a tag attached to a bag handle, a ring on a visible finger, or a small plant in a planter may be natural when the image supports it; these are conditional examples, not defaults. A mark on a printed motif must remain printed, not a physical object glued to a printed petal. Do not cover labels/windows or obstruct moving parts. Do not attach arbitrary bows, stickers or ornaments merely to obtain an add result.
2. Prefer a more suitable directly attached item over relocating the originally imagined item off the mask. Naturalness is a requirement, not something to trade away for contact. The new item can extend beyond the source mask and needs plausible contact and shadows; it need not fit entirely inside the source silhouette.
3. Only if direct additions are unnatural, consider a genuinely adjacent placement with a visible supporting surface and ONE uniquely determined side/site. Never use a remote landmark, a floating object, or vague 'near/beside' with several possible locations. Such an exception is anchor_mode=reference, needs resolved_execution_region_available=true supplied by preprocessing, and must retain its necessary placement in BOTH Ref and No-ref. Do not invent an execution mask or treat a large crop as one. With no resolved region, nearby add is unavailable in this pipeline; try another allowed operation or no_edit instead of forcing an unnatural accessory. With only add allowed, reject that instruction, not the source mask.
4. Direct attachment and host-local position are separate: "sewn onto the cuff of the sleeve" is support; "near the sleeve" is reference. Words such as below inside placement.site do not change a direct attachment into reference. Never leave dangling its/it host references in the item payload.
5. placement.relation describes the new item's relation to the selected anchor; a landmark inside ref_phrase merely identifies that anchor. Do not confuse these two relations. A bag beside a chair can still be a DIRECT anchor for a tag attached to the bag. Keep the final instruction short: item + direct relation + anchor, with a site only when required. Keep fallback reasons in skipped/evidence, not appended clauses.
"""

INSTRUCTION_STYLE += "\n\n" + ADD_ANCHOR_POLICY
